@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; A mark takes no paper from other flaps (decisions/a-line-reads-as-the-bundle-it-names). The corner .c folds
; onto the center, and --x is marked on that flap alone, along the diagonal:
; on the table it runs from the center to (3/4, 3/4). The layer beneath
; carries paper on the same table line from .a to (3/4, 3/4). The fold
; line of map .a onto .o crosses the diagonal at (1/4, 1/4), on the lower
; layer only, so --x lies on the side of the center and names it: that side
; stays and .a folds onto the center. Read as all the paper on its table
; line, --x would name no side.

paper square
mark (through .a .c) as --ac
.o = free on --ac from .a at 1/2
fold (map .c onto .o) (moving .c)
mark (through .a .c) (on #[.c]) as --x
fold (map .a onto .o) (toward --x)

; assert .a = (1/2, 1/2)
; assert .c = (1/2, 1/2)
; assert .b = (1, 0)
